      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-5,-8)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-5))^{2}+(y-(-8))^{2} & ={6}^{2} \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+(y+8)^{2} & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
